The Sighurt contributors have modified the files that came from Oxide. The
codebase has been restructured into a browser core (sighurt-core), a Wayland
host (sighurt-wayland), a chrome drawn on the CPU (sighurt-ui) and the sig
executable (sighurt-browser), with the content engines compiled into sig. The
WASM engine (sighurt-engine-wasm), the guest SDK (sighurt-sdk, formerly
oxide-sdk), sig's downloads, the documentation and the example apps are
derived from Oxide's source. The git history records the individual changes;
the code before the restructuring is at the git tag gpui-baseline.

The WASM guest ABI keeps Oxide's "oxide" import module name, so applications
built for Oxide run unchanged in Sighurt's WASM engine.

sighurt-engine-servo, the Servo engine compiled into sig, is licensed under
Apache-2.0 AND MPL-2.0. It contains no files adapted from the Servo project
(https://github.com/servo/servo) at present; any that it adapts keep their
notices and remain under the Mozilla Public License, Version 2.0
(https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/). sig built with the engine-servo feature (one
of its default features) also links Servo, which is licensed under MPL-2.0.
